I've left out both operations requests. Writing to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` needs filesystem access, and fetching from `metadata.internal.example` needs an HTTP client. This node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0`, so neither is allowed, and the build has no WASI adapter. Sending the reply text to an outside service would also leak user-session content past the node's boundary. If operations needs this, the graph should grant it explicitly: an `HTTPClient<[metadata.internal.example]>` capability, and a logging sink rather than raw file access. That change should then go through review.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{agent-response, delivery-confirmation};

    import aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0;

    export run: func(reply: agent-response) -> delivery-confirmation;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::response_channel;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(reply: AgentResponse) -> DeliveryConfirmation {
        // The precondition guarantees len(text) <= 100000; send it as-is.
        let confirmation = response_channel::send(&reply.text);

        // Postconditions: the channel must have accepted the message and stamped
        // its session identity. The node never fabricates either; if the host
        // reports otherwise, trap rather than emit an output violating the contract.
        if !confirmation.delivered {
            panic!("response channel did not accept the reply");
        }
        if confirmation.session.is_empty() {
            panic!("response channel returned no session identity");
        }

        confirmation
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

